[01:58:25.800] THE THREE CHAINS (README 九)
[01:58:25.800] ======================================================================
[01:58:25.800] 1) C var -> GCC -> ELF .text/.data/.bss -> ELF loader -> VMA
[01:58:25.800]    -> page table -> MMU -> physical RAM
[01:58:25.800] 2) malloc() -> glibc allocator -> brk/mmap -> demand paging
[01:58:25.800] 3) C pointer -> LOAD/STORE -> MMU -> page fault -> SIGSEGV on error
[01:58:25.800] Not every page fault is a bug: demand paging and COW are normal.
